    "optionsVersion": 1,
    "apiVersion": "VERSION_0",
    "isResourceIntensiveScript": false,
    "showPartitioning": false,
    "icon": "data:image/png;base64,",
    "description": "Histograms with automatic bin widths shared across groups, and distribution statistics (percentiles, skewness, kurtosis) per group.",
    "category": "Analytics",
    "subcategory": "Statistics",
    "tags": [
        "histogram",
        "distribution",
        "binning",
        "percentiles",
        "skewness",
        "descriptive statistics",
        "Freedman-Diaconis",
        "visokio-agents"
    ],
    "introductoryText": "Bins a numeric field into a **histogram**, overall or **per group**, with the bin width chosen automatically or by you, plus the **summary statistics** analysts look at next.\n\n- Bin width by the **Freedman-Diaconis** rule (twice the interquartile range over the cube root of the count; robust to outliers), **Sturges**, a number of bins, or a fixed width\n- The same bins for every group, so histograms line up; optionally clip the range to percentiles so a few extreme values do not squash the chart (values outside are counted as below or above range)\n- Statistics per group: count, missing, mean, standard deviation, minimum, P1, P5, quartiles, median, P95, P99, maximum, skewness and excess kurtosis",
    "dependencies": "",
